      "result": "# PWA-C6 source review: MUST FIX (one item)\n\n## MUST FIX\n\n**`src/app/operator/onboarding/OnboardingForm.tsx`, recovery group: the JSX does not compile.**\n\n```tsx\n{frozen && hasAttempt && <div className=\"topbar-actions\">\n  …\n</div>{showOfflineRecovery && <OfflineSubmissionNotice id={offlineRecoveryHint} purpose=\"recovery\" />}}\n```\n\nThe outer expression is now `frozen && hasAttempt && <div>…</div>{…}`. That is two adjacent JSX nodes inside one expression container. TypeScript reports TS2657 (\"JSX expressions must have one parent element\"), so the grouped build fails. If the claimed build/lint already passed, then the diff shown here is not what was built.\n\nMinimal fix: close the original group unchanged, then render the notice as a sibling. `showOfflineRecovery` already includes `frozen && hasAttempt`.\n\n```tsx\n    </div>}\n    {showOfflineRecovery && <OfflineSubmissionNotice id={offlineRecoveryHint} purpose=\"recovery\" />}\n```\n\nThis keeps the notice next to the recovery buttons and leaves every original condition intact. Re-run the grouped build/lint after fixing.\n\n## Checked and accepted\n\n**Classification form**\n- The submit guard runs before `setReviewRenewed(false)`.\n- The `renewReview` guard runs before `setRefreshing`, the fetch and review replacement.\n- When offline, `preventDefault` in `onSubmit` stops React's `action` from dispatching.\n- The hint shows only when `!pending && !refreshing`.\n\n**Attendance import**\n- Both the preview and commit guards run before `FormData`, `inFlight`, revision/attempt binding and `startTransition`.\n- File reading, header mapping, `invalidateSelection` and the reject download have no new guard.\n- The three hints each have their own `useId` and are gated on `!busy`.\n\n**Channel forms**\n- The guard runs before date conversion, `flight`, `setBusy`, `setMessage`, the mutation and the router.\n- The `!ready || busy` gate on the fieldset is unchanged.\n- The hint condition is `ready && !busy`.\n\n**Work policy**\n- `blockOfflineSubmission(event)` in `onSubmit` blocks `saveAction` when offline.\n- Fields, preview and the fieldset are unchanged.\n\n**Branding**\n- The guard runs before `setError('')` and the transition.\n- The hint condition is `canManage && !pending`, and the form only renders for `canManage`.\n\n**Operator action form**\n- The guard runs before the `ready`/`pending`/`inFlight` check, `FormData`, error and transition.\n\n**Onboarding (apart from the syntax error)**\n- The `dispatch` guard runs before the `captured` payload, intent, `inFlight`, phase and action.\n- A blocked attempt leaves phase, key and outcome untouched, so the original unknown/absent/actor-changed/replay rules still apply.\n- No storage, new key or automatic resend is added.\n- The editing notice requires `!frozen`. The recovery notice requires `frozen && hasAttempt` and is hidden while pending or unready. The saved state returns early.\n\n**Across all files**\n- Only the reviewed submit/review/recovery buttons gain `offline ||`.\n- Fieldsets and local editing/reading/navigation are untouched.\n- No global disable, queue or reload is added.\n- The online signal is not treated as proof that the service is reachable.\n\n## Non-blocking (no polish loop requested)\n\nThese need a fix only if lint fails on them:\n- Each file adds a second `import … from 'react'`.\n- The new lines use one-space indentation.\n- The parentheses in `offline || (busy)` are redundant.\n- `showOffline0/1/2` in the import form are three identical values.\n\n## Status\n\n- Source after the fix above: acceptable for C6 scope.\n- Both visuals: NOT VISUALLY VERIFIED.\n- Source review is not actual role, device or provider proof. Native, reference, provider, SQL, roles, device and full R0–R8 acceptance remain OPEN.",
