      "result": "**SOURCE ACCEPT**, for the syntax correction only (candidate `575ad432…925ce`).\n\n- **Parse:** The original `{frozen && hasAttempt && <div className=\"topbar-actions\">…</div>}` now closes before the notice. The notice is a separate sibling expression, so the TS2657 error is gone.\n- **Conditions:** `showOfflineRecovery = offline && ready && !pending && frozen && hasAttempt` contains the recovery group's own guard. So the notice can never appear without the recovery buttons. It stays hidden while pending or unready, and the saved state still returns early before it.\n- **Wiring:** Both recovery buttons still point `aria-describedby` at `offlineRecoveryHint` under the same `showOfflineRecovery` condition. The recovery wording, the frozen-page warning, the actor/key/unknown/absent replay rules and the original button conditions are unchanged.\n\nThis accepts the source only; nothing has been applied or built yet. The other six files are accepted on your statement that they are byte-unchanged; I did not compare hashes. After applying, the grouped build/lint still has to pass, and its result decides whether the duplicate `react` imports flagged earlier need changing.\n\nBoth visuals remain **NOT VISUALLY VERIFIED**. Native, reference, provider, SQL, roles, device and full R0–R8 acceptance remain **OPEN**.",
